{title: Twenty Pieces of Silver}
{subtitle: Genesis 37:12–36; 37:3–4; 39:2}
{key: F}
{tempo: 90}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [F] | [F] | [F] | [Dm] |
| [Dm] | [Bb] | [C] | [F] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
Jacob had twelve sons, but one he loved the best
The son of his [Dm]old age, set apart from all the rest
He made a [Bb]richly ornamented robe for him [C]to wear
And his [Bb]brothers couldn't speak a kind word [C]to him there
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
Out in the fields [F]of Dothan they saw him coming on
Here comes that [Dm]dreamer, let us kill him and be done
Reuben said [Bb]don't shed his blood, just [C]throw him in the pit
They [Bb]stripped him of his robe and they dropped him [C]down in it
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Twenty pieces of [F]silver
For their brother, their own flesh
On [Dm]a caravan to Egypt
With the balm and gum and myrrh
And [Bb]the boy who wore the [C]robe
Was a slave upon the [F]road
{end_of_chorus}

{comment: Interlude}
| [F] | [F] | [F] | [F] |
| [Dm] | [Dm] | [Bb] | [C] |
| [F] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
They dipped the robe in goat's blood and they sent it home to say
We found this, [Dm]is it your son's, and the old man turned away
It is [Bb]my son's robe, he cried, a [C]wild animal has torn him
[Bb]And he would not be comforted, [C]the father went on mourning
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Twenty pieces [F]of silver
For their brother, their own flesh
On a [Dm]caravan to Egypt
With the balm and gum and myrrh
And [Bb]the boy who wore the [C]robe
Was a slave upon the [F]road
{end_of_chorus}

{comment: Interlude}
| [F] | [F] | [F] | [F] |
| [Dm] | [Dm] | [Bb] | [C] |
| [F] | [F] |

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[Dm]Sold again in Egypt to Potiphar the guard
Far [Bb]from his father's tent and the fields of home so far
But the [Dm]brothers did not see it and the [C]boy did not yet know
The [Bb]LORD was with Joseph
[C]Everywhere that he would [F]go
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
Twenty pieces of silver
The LORD was with [Dm]Joseph
{end_of_verse}

